From afdce75a63abc7b1bb799d46a7cf994b18dbe355 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:30:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(avatars): fix same oval-distortion bug on public
 profile and podium photos
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Audited every other place in the app that renders a user's photoURL as a
circular avatar for the same display:grid + place-items:center + percentage
<img> bug just fixed on the main profile page (a non-stretched grid item's
percentage-sized image falls back to its own intrinsic aspect ratio instead
of the intended fixed square).

Two more spots had it:
- PublicProfile's .ppn-photo (the public/shareable profile page)
- AcademyRanking's .academy-podium-photo (top-3 podium avatars, used by
  PodiumTopThree)

Both fixed the same way: take the <img> out of grid track sizing with
position:absolute against the (already or newly) position:relative parent,
so object-fit:cover and border-radius:50% clip a true circle regardless of
the source photo's aspect ratio. Verified with a 9:16 test image in an
isolated Playwright harness before and after.

.nh-avatar (Home), .dc-avatar (ChallengesHubNew), .ch-new-avatar
(ChampionshipsNew) and .community-ranking-profile (CommunityRanking) were
also checked and are safe — they size their <img> with fixed pixel
dimensions, not percentages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GJxr5k2q4nCkbZphek1rFs
